    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "The suite is green \u2014 `AcceptanceTest` is the only test class, and it passes (along with a full `mvn test` BUILD SUCCESS).\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented idempotent owner creation on `POST /api/owners`: when a request repeats with an already-seen `Idempotency-Key` header, the originally created owner is replayed with 200 instead of creating a duplicate.\n\nTo keep structural impact low, I added behaviour as **small new cohesive units** (each a fresh class with zero surrounding complexity \u2014 `WMC_other = 0`) rather than growing any existing function, and touched only one existing file:\n\n**New files:**\n- `IdempotencyStore.java` \u2014 a `@Component` `ConcurrentHashMap<String, OwnerDto>` mapping key \u2192 first-created owner (`putIfAbsent`, first-writer-wins).\n- `CheckIdempotencyKey.java` \u2014 first pipeline step: reads the optional header via `ServerHttpConnection`, publishes it as a `String` variable (empty string = no key), and if the key is already known throws `IdempotentReplayException`.\n- `RecordIdempotencyKey.java` \u2014 after `save`, records the new owner's DTO under its key (no-op when no key).\n- `IdempotentReplayException.java` / `IdempotentReplayHandler.java` + its escalation YAML \u2014 the replay short-circuit responds 200 with the stored `OwnerDto`, reusing the existing escalation-handler convention.\n\n**Edited file:**\n- `owners.POST.yml` \u2014 wired `checkIdempotency` as the new entry step and `recordIdempotency` right after `save`.\n\nUsing an escalation for the replay path cleanly unwinds the pipeline (no double-response, no partial create), matching how the codebase already handles duplicate/conflict cases. The key variable is a unique type in the pipeline, so no `@Qualifier` was needed.",
