    "probe_text": "I've traced the entire pipeline. Here is the complete, ordered list of everything applied to `POST /api/owners`.\n\n## Endpoint guard (before any step)\n\n- **Authorization** \u2014 `composition.authorize: hasRole('OWNER_ADMIN')`. Callers without that role are rejected (403) before the pipeline runs.\n\nThe whole pipeline runs under a single `transaction` governance (`govern: [ transaction ]` on every step), so all the writes below commit once at the end.\n\n## The pipeline, in order\n\n1. **`checkIdempotency` \u2014 `CheckIdempotencyKey`**\n   - *Side-effect:* reads the optional `Idempotency-Key` header and publishes it (empty string = none) for later steps.\n   - *Short-circuit:* if that key was already used to create an owner, throws `IdempotentReplayException` \u2192 **replays the original owner with 200**, skipping the create entirely.\n\n2. **`build` \u2014 `BuildOwner`**\n   - *Side-effect:* publishes `sharesHousehold` (from `request.getSharesHousehold()`).\n   - *Side-effect:* composes/normalizes the address \u2014 either structured (`addressLine1` + `addressLine2`) or the legacy single `address` field.\n   - *Validation:* requires `firstName`, `lastName`, `address`, `city`, `telephone` all non-blank \u2192 else **400** (`MissingOwnerFieldsException`, listing the missing fields).\n   - *Side-effect:* maps DTO \u2192 `Owner`; **`registrationDate` defaults to today** if the request omitted it (via `OwnerMapper.toOwner`).\n   - *Validation + side-effect:* normalizes `telephone` to E.164 (assumes `+61`, strips a leading `0`, strips separators); invalid national-number length \u2192 **400** (`telephone`). Stores the normalized value.\n   - *Side-effect:* stores normalized `address`, and `addressLine1`/`addressLine2` when structured.\n   - *Validation:* if `email` present, must match the basic email regex \u2192 else **400** (`email`).\n   - Publishes the built `Owner`.\n\n3. **`checkEmailDomain` \u2014 `CheckEmailDomain`**\n   - *Validation:* if email's domain is a known disposable provider (`mailinator.com`, `tempmail.com`, `guerrillamail.com`) \u2192 **400** (`email`). Absent email is left untouched.\n\n4. **`validatePostcode` \u2014 `ValidatePostcode`**\n   - *Validation:* if a postcode is present it must be exactly 4 digits, and if the city has a known region it must fall in range (Sydney 2000\u20132099, Melbourne 3000\u20133099, Brisbane 4000\u20134099) \u2192 else **400** (`postcode`). Absent postcode / unknown city is allowed.\n\n5. **`assignHousehold` \u2014 `AssignHouseholdId`**\n   - *Side-effect:* sets a deterministic `householdId` = first 12 hex chars of SHA-256 over `normalize(lastName) | postcode`.\n\n6. **`checkHousehold` \u2014 `CheckUniqueHousehold`**\n   - *Validation:* unless `sharesHousehold=true`, if any other non-deleted owner already has the same `householdId` \u2192 **409** (`DuplicateHouseholdException`).\n\n7. **`checkIdentity` \u2014 `CheckUniqueIdentity`**\n   - *Validation:* if the full identity key `telephone | email | householdId` exactly matches another non-deleted owner \u2192 **409** (`DuplicateIdentityException`). (Same household with different phones is allowed.)\n\n8. **`checkCityCapacity` \u2014 `CheckCityCapacity`**\n   - *Validation:* if the owner's city (normalized) already holds \u2265 50 owners \u2192 **409** (`CityAtCapacityException`).\n\n9. **`adjustDate` \u2014 `AdjustRegistrationDate`**\n   - *Validation:* `registrationDate` must not be in the future \u2192 else **400** (`registrationDate`).\n   - *Side-effect:* rolls the date forward to the next business day, skipping Saturdays, Sundays, and the fixed 2026 holiday set.\n\n10. **`checkDailyLimit` \u2014 `CheckDailyLimit`**\n    - *Validation:* if \u2265 100 owners already share that (adjusted) `registrationDate` \u2192 **429** (`DailyOwnerLimitException`).\n\n11. **`assignCode` \u2014 `AssignCustomerCode`**\n    - *Side-effect:* sets `customerCode` = `<REGION>-<HASH8>`, where HASH8 is the first 8 upper-hex chars of SHA-256 over `telephone + lastName`.\n\n12. **`dedupeCode` \u2014 `DeduplicateCustomerCode`**\n    - *Side-effect:* if that `customerCode` collides with an existing owner, appends `-<n>` with the smallest `n \u2265 2` that makes it unique.\n\n13. **`countNamesakes` \u2014 `AssignNamesakeCount`**\n    - *Side-effect:* sets `namesakeCount` = number of existing owners sharing this first+last name (case-insensitive). The new owner isn't saved yet, so it counts only priors.\n\n14. **`flagBulkSignup` \u2014 `FlagBulkSignup`**\n    - *Side-effect:* sets `bulkSignupWarning = true` if > 80 owners already registered on that date.\n\n15. **`flagPossibleDuplicate` \u2014 `FlagPossibleDuplicate`**\n    - *Side-effect:* unless `sharesHousehold=true` or postcode is absent/blank, sets `possibleDuplicateOf` to the first existing owner with the same normalized lastName + same postcode but a *different* telephone.\n\n16. **`save` \u2014 `SaveOwner`**\n    - *Side-effect:* persists the owner (assigns its id).\n\n17. **`recordIdempotency` \u2014 `RecordIdempotencyKey`**\n    - *Side-effect:* if an `Idempotency-Key` was supplied, stores the owner's DTO under it so a repeat replays (step 1). No-op when no key.\n\n18. **`audit` \u2014 `AuditOwnerCreated`**\n    - *Side-effect:* emits an `AUDIT` log line with id, customerCode, registrationDate, membershipLevel, membershipNumber.\n\n19. **`respond` \u2014 `RespondWithOwnerCreated`**\n    - *Side-effect:* sends **201 Created** with `Location: /api/owners/{id}` and the `OwnerDto` body. `membershipLevel`, `membershipNumber`, `fiscalYear`, and `ageBand` are derived at mapping time (not stored on the entity).\n\n## Notes worth flagging\n\n- **Validation ordering caveat:** the CLAUDE.md guidance says to validate before loading so a bad body yields 400 not 404. Here `checkIdempotency` runs *first*, so a replayed idempotency key returns 200 even if the (ignored) body would have been invalid.\n- **Duplicate/capacity checks all scan `ownerRepository.findAll()`** in memory each time \u2014 several full-table scans per create.\n- The uniqueness checks (`CheckUniqueHousehold`, `CheckUniqueIdentity`, `DeduplicateCustomerCode`, capacity/limit counts) read committed state, but since everything shares one transaction and there's no locking, concurrent creates could race past them."
